        "author": "Marco Silva",
        "avatar": "avatar05",
        "time": "4:00 AM",
        "text": "This is an interesting article — maybe a bit dramatic in its framing, yet nonetheless it raises sharp points on team pace.",
        "linkText": "notes.marcosilva.org/p/why-small-teams-move-ahead",
        "unfurl": {
          "title": "Why small product teams are moving months ahead",
          "site": "notes.marcosilva.org",
          "text": "For ten years, a small group of practitioners predicted tighter loops between research and shipping. Now teams are seeing it firsthand.",
          "thumb": "unfurlSpeaker"
        },
        "replies": 2,
        "replyAvatars": ["avatar01", "avatar09"]
      },
      {
        "id": "m3",
        "author": "Nadia Okafor",
        "avatar": "avatar01",
        "time": "6:14 AM",
        "text": "Ran across a memorable phrase from a privacy researcher at Georgetown: “marketing by urgency”. Telling teams they have to adopt every tool overnight or fall behind? Yeah, that captures it.",
